# Kotlin Gray-Part — WebView Shell Spec

The WebView host (`StreamPortal`) must satisfy every TZ requirement below.

---

## WebSettings (baseline)

```kotlin
settings.apply {
    javaScriptEnabled = true                 // sites need JS
    domStorageEnabled = true                 // sessions / localStorage
    allowFileAccess = true
    allowContentAccess = true
    mediaPlaybackRequiresUserGesture = false // inline autoplay video
    mixedContentMode = MIXED_CONTENT_ALWAYS_ALLOW
    cacheMode = LOAD_DEFAULT
    setSupportMultipleWindows(true)          // target="_blank" handled in-app
    javaScriptCanOpenWindowsAutomatically = true
    userAgentString = buildUserAgent()       // see below
}
CookieManager.getInstance().apply {
    setAcceptCookie(true)
    setAcceptThirdPartyCookies(webView, true) // cookies / sessions
}
```

Activity in manifest: `windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize"`,
`hardwareAccelerated="true"`, `launchMode="singleTask"`,
`configChanges="orientation|screenSize|keyboardHidden|uiMode"`,
`screenOrientation="sensor"`.

---

## User-Agent

- Must NOT reveal a WebView (`; wv`) and must reflect the real device.
- For Zeus/Magma-style projects append the app identity suffix
  `appid/<bundleId> appname/<AppNamePascalCase>` as the LAST segment, used by
  BOTH the WebView and the OkHttp config client.

```kotlin
val base = "Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android ${Build.VERSION.RELEASE}; " +
    "${Build.BRAND} ${Build.MODEL.replace(" ","_")} Build/${Build.ID}) " +
    "AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) " +
    "Chrome/131.0.6778.135 Mobile Safari/537.36"
return "$base appid/$bundleId appname/$appNameToken"
```

---

## Safe area (notch / cutout) — required in BOTH orientations

- Manifest/window: `LAYOUT_IN_DISPLAY_CUTOUT_MODE_SHORT_EDGES`.
- Apply padding via `setOnApplyWindowInsetsListener`:
  - **portrait** → top inset (status bar + top notch),
  - **landscape** → left + right insets (side cameras).
- Re-apply on `onConfigurationChanged` and after lock/unlock.
- The CSS safe-area kill in the page is SEPARATE and must NOT use `*` selectors
  (see pitfalls #10) — only `:root` vars + named root containers.

---

## Keyboard must not cover inputs (3 layers, all required)

1. Manifest: `windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize"` (not adjustPan).
2. Don't fight it from native layout (no manual resize on top of adjustResize).
3. JS inject: on `focusin` + `visualViewport.resize`, after ~350ms
   `el.scrollIntoView({behavior:'auto', block:'center'})` — `auto`, never
   `smooth` (smooth fights the keyboard animation and causes jitter).

---

## Redirect loop (ERR_TOO_MANY_REDIRECTS)

Track the last main-frame URL in `shouldOverrideUrlLoading`. On
`onReceivedError` for the main frame with code `-9`/`-1007` or
"too_many_redirects", reload the last URL, up to 3 times, before giving up.

---

## shouldOverrideUrlLoading routing

```kotlin
when {
    u.startsWith("http") || u.startsWith("about") ||
    u.startsWith("data") || u.startsWith("blob") -> false  // stay in WebView
    u.startsWith("tel:") || u.startsWith("mailto:") || u.startsWith("sms:") ||
    u.startsWith("market:") || u.startsWith("intent:") ||
    u.startsWith("whatsapp:") -> { startActivity(VIEW intent); true }
    else -> false  // unknown → keep in WebView (don't bounce to Chrome)
}
```
Deep links the WebView can't handle: catch and hand to the system via
`Intent.ACTION_VIEW`, then keep the user on the previous page so they don't see
an error on return.

---

## target="_blank" / window.open

`onCreateWindow` must load into the SAME WebView (never spawn an external tab):
```kotlin
override fun onCreateWindow(view: WebView, dialog: Boolean,
        gesture: Boolean, msg: Message): Boolean {
    (msg.obj as? WebView.WebViewTransport)?.apply {
        webView = view; msg.sendToTarget()
    }
    return true
}
```

---

## File upload (no storage permission)

`WebChromeClient.onShowFileChooser` → launch `params.createIntent()` via an
`ActivityResultContracts.StartActivityForResult` launcher, return the result
with `FileChooserParams.parseResult`. Camera/gallery work through the chooser.

---

## Back navigation

`OnBackPressedCallback`: if `webView.canGoBack()` → `goBack()`, else do nothing
(back on the first page must NOT close the app). System back + gestures both
route through this.

---

## Offline detection (see pitfalls #11)

- `NetWire.connectivityFlow` via `registerDefaultNetworkCallback`
  (`onLost`/`onUnavailable` → false) collected in the WebView screen.
- A ~4s heartbeat that checks `isConnected()` for the "page already loaded, then
  internet dropped" case.
- On offline: blank the WebView (`about:blank`) then open OfflinePortal with the
  current URL as the return target. Retry reloads it (handle in `onNewIntent`).

---

## Push URL into the WebView (one-time)

- `PushBus.onWarmUrl` is set in `StreamPortal.onStart`, cleared in
  `onStop`/`onDestroy`.
- `PushRelay.onMessageReceived`: if `PushBus.onWarmUrl != null` and the payload
  has a `url` → call it (loads into the live WebView) and DON'T show a
  notification / DON'T persist. Otherwise save `coldPushUrl` and post a
  notification.
- Cold start: `WelcomePortal` consumes `coldPushUrl` BEFORE the state machine
  and opens the WebView on it. Warm tap while running → `onNewIntent` loads it.
- Never persist a push URL beyond its one-time use.
